WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.620 --> 00:00:05.640
September is coming in strong on Netflix with
more than 30 original new shows, movies, and

00:00:05.640 --> 00:00:06.540
comedy specials.

00:00:06.640 --> 00:00:10.570
With that many selections the casual viewer
is going to have a hard time picking out new

00:00:10.570 --> 00:00:15.429
favorites, so we went through everything coming
to Netflix in September 2019 to find the best

00:00:15.429 --> 00:00:16.200
of the best.

00:00:16.920 --> 00:00:21.440
Just because Sacha Baron Cohen is headlining
the Netflix original limited series The Spy

00:00:21.440 --> 00:00:23.500
doesn't mean you should expect a ridiculous
comedy.

00:00:23.640 --> 00:00:28.210
The star of such films as Borat and The Dictator
has always hidden social commentary beneath

00:00:28.210 --> 00:00:32.759
his outrageous characters, but this time he's
tapping into his more serious side to portray

00:00:32.759 --> 00:00:37.600
Israeli intelligence operative Eli Cohen,
who infiltrated the Syrian political system

00:00:37.600 --> 00:00:41.240
in the early '60s before ultimately suffering
a public execution.

00:00:41.440 --> 00:00:44.620
You can check out The Spy when all six episodes
land on September 6.

00:00:45.660 --> 00:00:49.740
This drama about a murder at a prestigious
boarding school pulled in rave reviews when

00:00:49.740 --> 00:00:54.690
it was released on Netflix in October 2018,
with critics calling it a "must watch series"

00:00:54.690 --> 00:00:58.500
and praising everything from the pacing to
its deft handling of sensitive topics.

00:00:58.760 --> 00:01:01.060
But for all that, Elite never quite gained
a foothold.

00:01:01.400 --> 00:01:03.180
Maybe because it's a Spanish-language show?

00:01:03.460 --> 00:01:06.440
Maybe because it looks like any other dime-a-dozen
high-school melodrama?

00:01:06.600 --> 00:01:09.100
Well, don't let those surface impressions
slow you down.

00:01:09.260 --> 00:01:13.500
Elite is a smart, brutal drama, and there's
never been a better time to check it out,

00:01:13.500 --> 00:01:14.540
subtitles and all.

00:01:14.720 --> 00:01:18.580
It's no surprise that Netflix bet their money
on a second season of Elite, which debuts

00:01:18.580 --> 00:01:19.580
on September 6th.

00:01:20.400 --> 00:01:24.320
English actor and comedian Jack Whitehall
brings an enthusiasm to the stage that's hard

00:01:24.330 --> 00:01:28.810
not to get behind, and that same excitement
shows up in Netflix's Jack Whitehall: Travels

00:01:28.810 --> 00:01:33.220
with My Father, which sees Whitehall and his
dad hit up exotic locales in an attempt to

00:01:33.220 --> 00:01:34.280
bond with each other.

00:01:34.540 --> 00:01:35.940
"I'm just trying to be a good son.

00:01:36.480 --> 00:01:38.400
… He's a very nice boy, Jack.

00:01:39.520 --> 00:01:40.460
He's just a bit thick."

00:01:41.020 --> 00:01:45.100
Audiences got a kick out of the first two
seasons, which saw the Whitehalls visiting

00:01:45.110 --> 00:01:49.420
South Asia and Eastern Europe, and fans of
the show are no doubt looking forward to another

00:01:49.420 --> 00:01:53.260
comedic adventure with season 3, which arrives
on Netflix on September 6th.

00:01:54.420 --> 00:01:56.080
What is The I-Land, exactly?

00:01:56.320 --> 00:01:59.970
All we know is that the show happens on an
island, things get crazy, and someone's watching

00:01:59.970 --> 00:02:00.720
it all go down.

00:02:00.990 --> 00:02:04.660
Kate Bosworth is starring and the premise
sets up a group of strangers who wake up on

00:02:04.660 --> 00:02:07.260
a mysterious island with no idea how they
got there.

00:02:07.690 --> 00:02:12.000
Judging by the trailer for the series, things
take a hard left turn into chaos after that,

00:02:12.000 --> 00:02:14.780
leaving these strangers fighting and running
for their lives.

00:02:14.900 --> 00:02:19.280
There's a little sci-fi, a little horror,
and a whole lot of mystery, and you can experience

00:02:19.290 --> 00:02:21.560
it all when The I-Land premieres on September
12th.

00:02:22.810 --> 00:02:27.660
Funny or Die's Between Two Ferns with Zach
Galifianakis probably doesn't need an introduction,

00:02:27.660 --> 00:02:32.510
but for the uninitiated, it's basically this:
Zach Galifianakis kind of interviews celebrities

00:02:32.510 --> 00:02:35.820
on a low budget set that includes, believe
it or not, two ferns.

00:02:36.020 --> 00:02:40.200
He's interviewed everyone from Barack Obama
to Bradley Cooper, and the results are always

00:02:40.200 --> 00:02:40.700
hilarious.

00:02:41.060 --> 00:02:41.920
"Are you nominated?

00:02:42.200 --> 00:02:42.880
I, uh, yeah.

00:02:43.200 --> 00:02:43.920
For what?

00:02:44.280 --> 00:02:46.520
For best actor.

00:02:47.380 --> 00:02:48.660
How's bragging camp going?"

00:02:50.920 --> 00:02:55.170
It's high time the oddball web series saw
a revival, and we can thank Netflix for making

00:02:55.170 --> 00:02:55.740
it happen.

00:02:55.980 --> 00:03:00.080
According to Deadline, Between Two Ferns:
The Movie is being imagined as a sort of meta

00:03:00.099 --> 00:03:04.870
mockumentary starring Galifianakis as a version
of himself who lost all credibility when Will

00:03:04.870 --> 00:03:07.360
Ferrell uploaded Between Two Ferns to Funny
Or Die.

00:03:07.590 --> 00:03:11.500
In a last bid to fix his reputation, Zach's
hitting the road with his show so that he

00:03:11.519 --> 00:03:15.160
can finally become a real talk show host and
get everybody to stop laughing at him.

00:03:15.160 --> 00:03:18.300
We can't wait to check it out when it hits
Netflix on September 20th.

00:03:19.280 --> 00:03:23.140
In one of the most ambitious series Netflix
has ever offered, Criminal follows multiple

00:03:23.150 --> 00:03:26.790
storylines across four different countries
- in four different languages - and they're

00:03:26.790 --> 00:03:27.540
each their own show​.

00:03:27.700 --> 00:03:31.519
There aren't many details out at this time,
but it appears that Criminal will consist

00:03:31.519 --> 00:03:37.120
of 12 stories that mainly center around police
interrogation rooms in the UK, France, Germany,

00:03:37.120 --> 00:03:37.620
and Spain.

00:03:37.700 --> 00:03:41.680
David Tennant headlines the UK cast and the
whole shebang drops on September 20.

00:03:42.780 --> 00:03:46.740
There's a killer on the loose in Netflix's
upcoming thriller In the Shadow of the Moon,

00:03:46.740 --> 00:03:49.540
and it's up to a Philadelphia cop to bring
him to justice.

00:03:49.720 --> 00:03:53.840
Predator's Boyd Holbrook stars as the police
officer who's leading the hunt for the mysterious

00:03:53.840 --> 00:03:54.340
murderer.

00:03:54.420 --> 00:03:57.580
His only clue is that the killer times their
crimes to the lunar cycle.

00:03:57.820 --> 00:04:02.800
"Moon bike...what is that?

00:04:03.400 --> 00:04:04.220
Moon bike?

00:04:04.880 --> 00:04:06.320
I said a lunar cycle."

00:04:06.700 --> 00:04:10.680
Dexter's Michael C. Hall has also joined the
cast in an as-yet unnamed role.

00:04:10.980 --> 00:04:14.040
Look for In the Shadow of the Moon on September
27th.

00:04:14.880 --> 00:04:19.440
American Horror Story co-creator Ryan Murphy
is back with a new show: The Politician, a

00:04:19.440 --> 00:04:22.500
violent political comedy set in a California
high school.

00:04:22.500 --> 00:04:26.889
Murphy is teaming up with his longtime AHS
partner Brad Falchuk to tell the story of

00:04:26.889 --> 00:04:31.660
Payton Hobart, a teenager with dreams of one
day becoming the president of the United States.

00:04:31.760 --> 00:04:35.180
Before he conquers the White House, however,
he'll have to conquer the politics of his

00:04:35.180 --> 00:04:36.080
local high school.

00:04:36.400 --> 00:04:41.419
Ben Platt starts as Payton, with an exciting
supporting cast that includes AHS veterans

00:04:41.420 --> 00:04:46.680
Jessica Lange and Dylan McDermott, along with
Zoey Deutch, Bette Midler, and Gwyneth Paltrow.

00:04:46.920 --> 00:04:50.760
Judging by the trailer, The Politician is
going to be a laugh out loud dark comedy.

00:04:51.180 --> 00:04:52.140
"Think I should kill him?

00:04:52.760 --> 00:04:53.260
What?

00:04:57.140 --> 00:04:58.260
….yes, yes I do."

00:04:58.920 --> 00:05:00.600
Look for it on September 27th.

00:05:01.480 --> 00:05:05.080
Netflix is bringing out a handful of new comedy
specials in September.

00:05:05.080 --> 00:05:09.080
Keep your eyes peeled for Bill Burr: Paper
Tiger, which sees the irreverent comedian

00:05:09.080 --> 00:05:12.960
taking on topics that range from Michelle
Obama's book tour to his own marriage.

00:05:13.180 --> 00:05:14.740
You can catch that on September 10.

00:05:15.040 --> 00:05:19.650
On the 24th, look for Jeff Dunham: Beside
Himself for the only comedy hour with puppets

00:05:19.650 --> 00:05:20.320
you'll ever need.

00:05:20.460 --> 00:05:23.580
Well, except for Dunham's five other Netflix
comedy specials, that is.

00:05:24.080 --> 00:05:28.660
Finally, September 30 sees the first Netflix
offering from English stand-up comedian Mo

00:05:28.660 --> 00:05:30.700
Gilligan, a special titled Momentum.

00:05:30.880 --> 00:05:34.740
That does it for all the great Netflix originals
hitting the streaming service in September

00:05:34.740 --> 00:05:35.680
2019.

00:05:36.060 --> 00:05:39.380
Now let's pivot to see what other movies and
shows are going to be worth watching this

00:05:39.380 --> 00:05:39.880
month.

00:05:40.660 --> 00:05:44.180
There are a ton of must-watch action movies
storming onto Netflix in September.

00:05:44.260 --> 00:05:48.639
The streaming service is heating up its lineup
with 300 and Dante's Peak, for starters.

00:05:48.639 --> 00:05:52.420
It's also bringing in two thirds of the Lord
of the Rings trilogy - The Two Towers and

00:05:52.420 --> 00:05:53.380
The Return of the King.

00:05:53.640 --> 00:05:55.620
All of those films arrive on the first of
the month.

00:05:55.840 --> 00:05:59.880
And on the 26th, you can check out the martial
arts action epic The Grandmaster.

00:05:59.890 --> 00:06:03.870
On the thriller side of things, look for American
Psycho on the first, which marks Christian

00:06:03.870 --> 00:06:08.720
Bale's transformative role as fictional serial
killer and all-around whackjob Patrick Bateman.

00:06:09.040 --> 00:06:13.699
Netflix is also adding Come and Find Me, a
2016 film starring Aaron Paul as a man on

00:06:13.700 --> 00:06:15.000
the hunt for his missing girlfriend.

00:06:15.320 --> 00:06:18.760
If you're more of a monsters in the closet
kind of person, you won't be disappointed.

00:06:19.020 --> 00:06:24.160
September 1 sees the arrival of The Last Exorcism,
while the 13th heralds Head Count, a creature

00:06:24.160 --> 00:06:28.440
feature about a shape-shifting monster chowing
down on a bunch of teens in the desert.

00:06:28.860 --> 00:06:32.620
From slow-burning mysteries to tearjerker
dramedies, there's going to be something for

00:06:32.620 --> 00:06:34.420
everyone in the drama category.

00:06:34.439 --> 00:06:39.289
The month opens with Clint Eastwood's Oscar-winning
Mystic River, J.D. Salinger biopic Rebel in

00:06:39.289 --> 00:06:40.980
the Rye, and The Lake House.

00:06:41.240 --> 00:06:44.460
Most of what we're getting in the comedy genre
is stuff we've seen a dozen times, but that

00:06:44.740 --> 00:06:47.160
doesn't mean they don't merit a casual rewatch.

00:06:47.160 --> 00:06:52.080
Superbad is popping up on the service, which
was pretty much the comedy to watch in 2007.

00:06:52.280 --> 00:06:53.220
Haven't seen it in awhile?

00:06:53.400 --> 00:06:55.700
You may just find yourself McLovin it all
over again.

00:06:56.140 --> 00:06:59.139
If you're in the right mood, you can also
look for You Don't Mess with the Zohan.

00:06:59.140 --> 00:07:01.900
Both that and Superbad arrive on the first
of the month.

00:07:02.800 --> 00:07:07.080
Netflix is bringing a ton of much awaited
seasons of network shows into the fold, which

00:07:07.090 --> 00:07:10.880
is great news for anyone who watches TV exclusively
on streaming services.

00:07:10.880 --> 00:07:13.759
Is it worth it to wait a year for the next
season of American Horror Story?

00:07:13.759 --> 00:07:18.410
It never seems like it at the time, but now
that AHS: Apocalypse is slipping onto Netflix

00:07:18.410 --> 00:07:21.480
on September 24, the wait feels a little more
bearable.

00:07:21.480 --> 00:07:26.200
Other shows we can look forward to in September
include Season 9 of The Walking Dead and Season

00:07:26.210 --> 00:07:28.280
3 of MTV's Scream, both on the first.

00:07:28.280 --> 00:07:32.639
We're following that up with Season 9 of Shameless
on the 10th and Season 5 of Gotham on the

00:07:32.640 --> 00:07:33.140
30th.

00:07:34.260 --> 00:07:36.220
Check out one of our newest videos right here!

00:07:36.460 --> 00:07:39.660
Plus, even more Looper videos about your favorite
shows are coming soon.

00:07:39.800 --> 00:07:43.760
Subscribe to our YouTube channel and hit the
bell so you don't miss a single one.

